{
    "background_story": "Eithan was a young, brilliant scholar who had dedicated his life to studying the ancient texts of the Hebrew Bible. Growing up in a family of rabbis, he was fascinated by the intricacies of the Masoretic tradition, which preserved the precise pronunciation and cantillation of the sacred texts. Eithan spent years pouring over the manuscripts, learning the complex system of vowels, accents, and punctuation that brought the words to life. His expertise earned him a coveted spot at the prestigious Jerusalem Academy, where he worked alongside renowned scholars to decipher and translate rare manuscripts. Eithan's passion for the Masoretic tradition not only deepened his understanding of the scriptures but also inspired a new generation of students to explore the rich heritage of Jewish scholarship.",
